FFF][/dim]prompts/202609/usage_collector_health_and_drift_resilience.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-yz[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-yz/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Collector health domain model in the Rust core[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]health-core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]health-core: track failure-streak start in the refresh schedule, project[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a per-provider collector_health block into the public snapshot, gate and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]re-rank CollectionProblem attention on consistent failure, add the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]vendor_drift reason code, and coordinate the sase-core release plus the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-side floor bump.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Drift-classifying probe strategies for all collectors[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]drift-probes[dim] · [dim][/dim]after health-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]drift-probes: add a shared bounded probe-strategy runner with drift [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]classification, adopt it in the Claude, Codex, and Grok collectors, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]annotate fallback recoveries on ok observations, and extend the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]live-mirroring fixtures to cover strategy chains and drift [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]classification.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Collector health in the usage CLI and doctor[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]health-cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after health-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]health-cli: render collector health in sase usage list status cells and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]verbose records, pass it through --json, add shared pure health [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]label/style helpers, and flag consistently failing collectors in sase [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]doctor.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Failing-collector indicator across ACE surfaces[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]health-tui[dim] · [dim][/dim]after health-core, health-cli[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]health-tui: give the failing-collector state one visual identity (glyph,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]color, wording) and render it in the Providers Usage view rows and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]detail header, the top-bar usage indicator and tooltip, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]picker/models-panel capacity hints, with updated visual goldens and no [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]new refresh paths.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Integrated verification, live smoke, and docs[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]health-verify[dim] · [dim][/dim]after health-core, drift-probes, health-cli, health-tui[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]health-verify: run the combined acceptance checks including check-full [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through a monitor, perform a bounded live smoke plus an induced-failure [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]walkthrough on an isolated SASE_HOME, and document collector health and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the indicator.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-yz","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-yz.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-150ceddee45af9503a3948915307e289","started_at":"2026-09-09T16:41:07.157759+00:00","state":"completed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":